Clarte eye tracking: freeze the pose input weights during calibration (prototypes/Eye Tracking)
==============================================================================================

Freeze-only subset of gaze-lab/patches/clarte-eye-tracking-fixes.patch (the WebEyeTrack.ts hunks, unchanged), for Clarte
commit b7b8f98f169f71a7c87e31d71cade3df06c6b3af; vendor/webeyetrack/local/WebEyeTrack.ts is unchanged on origin/main since.
Review material only; nothing has been applied anywhere. From the Clarte repo root:
  git apply --check gaze-lab/patches/clarte-eye-tracking-freeze-only.patch

What it changes: in WebEyeTrack.adapt(), the gradient of the first Dense layer's kernel rows 512-517 (the head-vector and
face-origin inputs) is zeroed at every Adam step (tf.variableGrads + masked applyGradients); loss, optimizer, hold-out and
early stopping are otherwise as shipped. With 42 labels at one pose those inputs are constant, so unfrozen they act as a
free bias and the pretrained head-movement compensation is lost to whatever the training trajectory does.

Why this subset: the matrix-layout correction in the full patch made the shipped (pretrained) network WORSE on both recorded
sessions (pooled +14 px [+5, +23] and +21 px [+10, +32]; translation and head-turn blocks), so it should not ship with the
current weights. No MODEL_VERSION bump is needed for this subset: the head vector is unchanged; existing saved calibrations
keep working (they were trained without the freeze and keep their own weights until the person recalibrates).

Measured (one tester, gaze-lab): live session 2, frozen head from session 1 vs fresh shipped calibration on the same frames:
10 cm slide left 14.0 cm -> 2.4 cm median error, right 10.7 -> 3.2 cm. Video replay of both sessions with the fix vs without
(paired per dot, 95 % bootstrap): session 2 pooled -127 px [-161, -92], 88/111 dots better, no block worse; session 1 pooled
-0.3 px [-2, +1] (that calibration happened not to drift). Details: gaze-lab/REPLAY-FIXES-REPORT.md, EYE-TRACKING-PLAN.md.
Regenerate vendor/webeyetrack/LOCAL-ADAPTATIONS.patch and the source fingerprint after applying (repo convention).

--- "a/prototypes/Eye Tracking/vendor/webeyetrack/local/WebEyeTrack.ts"
